# The natural-language-to-scryfall-filters service backing /magic-tools is
# reached same-origin at /api — the Vite dev server proxies it to localhost:8080
# and Firebase Hosting rewrites it to Cloud Run in production — so this is
# normally left unset.
#
# Setting it points a local build at a deployed instance, which is a
# cross-origin call — and the service no longer sends CORS headers at all, so
# a browser will block that. Use it for curl or a non-browser client; to
# exercise a deployed backend from the site, change the Vite proxy target
# instead and stay same-origin.
# VITE_TRANSLATE_API_URL=https://your-service.run.app

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The music section's two source cards.
#
# Read by scripts/fetch-music.mjs, which runs as the first step of `npm run
# build` and writes src/content/music.generated.json plus the cover art under
# public/images/music/. Both are committed, so a clone without these variables
# still builds — it just ships the last snapshot instead of a fresh one.
#
# Deliberately NOT prefixed VITE_: these must never reach the bundle. A public
# page cannot hold a secret, so the fetch happens at build time on a trusted
# machine and only the resulting data is published.

# From an app you create at https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard, with
# http://127.0.0.1:8888/callback as a redirect URI. Run
# `node scripts/spotify-auth.mjs` once to mint the refresh token.
#
# The owning account needs an active Spotify Premium subscription: since
# 9 March 2026 Development Mode apps stop working without one, and a personal
# site can never leave Development Mode (Extended Quota is businesses only,
# 250k+ monthly actives). If Premium lapses, the build warns and the Spotify
# card freezes on its last snapshot.
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_ID=
# SPOTIFY_CLIENT_SECRET=
# SPOTIFY_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# The numeric fan id, visible in the data-blob of your own bandcamp.com/<user>
# page. No key or login is needed — Bandcamp has no official API for a fan
# collection, so this reads the same undocumented endpoint the fan page itself
# calls, which can change without notice.
# BANDCAMP_FAN_ID=
